.nh
.TH "GH-ISSUE-ARTIFACT-DELETE" "1" "Oct 2026" "GitHub CLI 2.103.3" "GitHub CLI manual"

.SH NAME
gh-issue-artifact-delete - Delete issue artifacts (preview)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgh issue artifact delete {<issue> <artifact-number>... | <artifact-url>...} [flags]\fR


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete artifacts from an issue. A deleted artifact can't be restored.

.PP
Name artifacts by their issue and numbers, or by their URLs, which must all be
on one issue. \fB<issue>\fR is an issue number or URL.

.PP
In a terminal, deletion requires confirmation. \fB--yes\fR skips the prompt and is
required when prompting is unavailable.


.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--yes\fR
Confirm deletion without prompting


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
.TP
\fB-R\fR, \fB--repo\fR \fB<[HOST/]OWNER/REPO>\fR
Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format


.SH EXIT CODES
0: Successful execution

.PP
1: Error

.PP
2: Command canceled

.PP
4: Authentication required

.PP
NOTE: Specific commands may have additional exit codes. Refer to the command's help for more information.


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
# Delete artifact 2 from issue 142
$ gh issue artifact delete 142 2

# Delete two artifacts without a prompt
$ gh issue artifact delete 142 2 5 --yes

.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgh-issue-artifact(1)\fR
